	"notes": "Shopify's developer docs use the classic three-part shape — a top bar, a list of every doc on the left, the page you are reading on the right — but the left list has an extra middle step most sites skip: on a laptop it shrinks to a thin strip of icons instead of disappearing, and only expands to full labelled links on a bigger desktop monitor. The more interesting part is the article text itself: no matter how wide the screen gets, the scan measures it at exactly 810 pixels wide every single time, simply centred in whatever room is left next to the sidebar. That is why the grid of 'App Home', 'Checkout UI extensions' and other cards always shows two columns on any desktop screen and never more, even on the widest monitor tested — the box they live in never grows. On a phone the sidebar disappears behind a menu button and the cards stack into one column.",
